From: NeoDarwin
Subject: [PATCH] nano_zone: give arm64 the v1 address layout

The published nano_zone.h keeps the nano v1 address-field layout for x86_64
only and stops with #error on any other architecture, though platform.h
enables CONFIG_NANOZONE for every 64-bit target. arm64 allocates through
nano v2 (nanov2_malloc.c), and nothing outside nano_zone.h uses the v1
layout, so arm64 takes x86_64's widths; they only have to compile.

Rebase-risk: low (one condition).
---
diff --git a/src/nano_zone.h b/src/nano_zone.h
--- a/src/nano_zone.h
+++ b/src/nano_zone.h
@@ -33,7 +33,7 @@
 
 /*************          nanozone address field layout        ******************/
 
-#if defined(__x86_64)
+#if defined(__x86_64) || defined(__arm64__) /* NeoDarwin: v1 is unused on arm64 (nano v2) */
 #define NANO_MAG_BITS			6
 #define NANO_BAND_BITS			17
 #define NANO_SLOT_BITS			4
